




## Terminology mapping: paper names vs code names

The paper and the code use slightly different names in a few places. This table is the quickest way to translate between them.

| Paper term                        | Code / CLI term                                              |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Bifocal scheduler**             | `hefthint`                                                   |
| **Weight Layout Arbiter**         | `weight-suggest`                                             |
| **Linear** layout                 | `ND`                                                         |
| **NPU_OPT** layout                | `NZ`                                                         |
| **PIM_OPT** layout                | `PIM-OPT`                                                    |
| **Dual copy**                     | `DUAL`                                                       |
| **Prefill–decode partition (PD)** | `pd` baseline                                                |
| **Attention-on-PIM baseline**     | `attn_on_pim` or `attacc` depending on the granularity you want |
| **FACIL-inspired decode rule**    | `facil`                                                      |
| **IANUS-inspired decode rule**    | `ianus`                                                      |
| **NeuPIMs-inspired rule**         | `neupims`                                                    |

### Built-in baseline policies

The current baseline registry includes the following policy names:

| Baseline         | Code behavior                                                |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `pd`             | Prefill on NPU, decode on PIM.                               |
| `weights_on_pim` | Weight-bearing operators on PIM; the rest on NPU/CPU.        |
| `attn_on_pim`    | Attention-related operators on PIM.                          |
| `ianus`          | Prefill on NPU; decode keeps Q/K/Softmax/Norm/Add off PIM and offloads most other work. |
| `neupims`        | Prefill on NPU; decode offloads `QK`, `SV`, and KV-read/write-style work to PIM. |
| `attacc`         | Prefill on NPU; decode offloads `QK`, `SV`, `Softmax`, and KV-read/write-style work to PIM. |
| `facil`          | Prefill on NPU; decode offloads GEMV-like operators and `QK`/`SV` to PIM. |

